# jarvis-browse

State the whole task as one goal and run it with `exec`:

```bash
node %RUNNER% --goal "find out whether sandhya replied to my last email"
```

Optionally say where to start:

```bash
node %RUNNER% --goal "what time does the British Library close today" --url "https://www.bl.uk"
```

The output is the answer, grounded in the pages it actually read. Quote it —
the dates, addresses and wording in it come from the real pages.

## Rules

- Pass the user's own words in the goal when the task is saying something to
  someone — their words are what authorises sending.
- One call per task. The tool follows links, searches and fills forms itself;
  do not break the task into page-level steps.
- If it reports a refusal (a sign-in page, a password field, something outside
  what the user asked), relay that and stop. Do not work around it with any
  other tool.
